]` and the C smashes its stack — every C build (-O0/-O1/-O2) dies with SIGSEGV and prints nothing. That's undefined behavior with no reproducible output, so the Rust uses a 1024-byte backing store (documented in `main.rs`), which reproduces C exactly for all inputs where the overflow doesn't hit the return address, and keeps computing instead of faulting beyond that."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":947,"cache_read_input_tokens":65655,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":947,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06552a30-eea7-4d45-9162-d7a720b04073","uuid":"1ae31a0d-355c-436b-befa-48fa563ec47f","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:46:46.462Z"}
